# 🛒 SuperKart Sales Forecasting

An end-to-end Machine Learning application for predicting product sales revenue for SuperKart stores.

The project covers the complete ML lifecycle:

- Exploratory Data Analysis
- Feature Engineering
- Data Preprocessing
- Machine Learning Model Development
- Hyperparameter Optimization
- Model Evaluation
- Model Serialization
- REST API Development
- Streamlit Frontend
- Docker Containerization
- Cloud Deployment using Render

---

## 🚀 Live Application

### 🌐 Frontend Application

The deployed Streamlit application is available at:

https://superkart-sales-forecasting-1.onrender.com

Use this URL to interact with the sales prediction application.

### 🔌 Backend API

The Flask REST API is deployed separately at:

https://superkart-sales-forecasting.onrender.com

The frontend communicates with this backend to generate predictions.

---

## 📌 Project Overview

SuperKart is a retail organization operating multiple stores across different cities and regions.

The objective of this project is to develop a machine learning solution that can predict the expected sales revenue of a product in a particular store.

Accurate sales forecasting can help businesses with:

- Inventory planning
- Product assortment optimization
- Store-level planning
- Revenue forecasting
- Demand analysis
- Business decision-making

The final solution uses an optimized Random Forest Regression model and exposes the trained model through a REST API.

---

